    <Fact path="/scopedStateOptions">
      <Name>The options for deciding which U.S. jurisdiction a filer lived and earned in</Name>
      <Description>Every U.S. jurisdiction the Form 1040 instructions name individually - the 50
        states and the District of Columbia - plus moreThanOne for a filer with income in several
        of them, plus noneOfThese for the instructions' remaining "Where Do You File?" row.

        THE LIST IS NOT A SCOPE LINE. It used to be one: 25 states and no DC,
        with everything else answering noneOfThese and refused at submission. State of residence
        is never a ground for refusing a federal 1040 (project invariant #7 as amended), so the
        members below are exactly the jurisdictions the instructions print, and this fact is
        a VOCABULARY rather than a boundary. It is byte-for-byte /statesAndDistrictsOptions
        (constants.xml:295) with moreThanOne prepended and noneOfThese appended, in that fact's
        own order, so the two move together by construction rather than by prose.

        noneOfThese IS NOT "an unsupported state". Once all 51 jurisdictions are members
        it means precisely the instructions' fifth filing row: a foreign country, a U.S.
        territory, or an APO or FPO address. filers:/flowKnockoutUnsupportedState still refuses
        that answer, because a bona fide resident of a U.S. possession does not file a plain 1040. Intake separates the
        two populations:
        filers:/filers/*/writableIsBonaFidePossessionResident asks a No/Yes per filer,
        and the guard releases a noneOfThese return only once every filer it asks has answered No.
        A SECOND CONTRADICTION IS CLOSED WITH IT: a primary who answers No here but whose Schedule
        8812 intake separately attests a bona fide Puerto Rico residence
        (ctcOdc:/writableIsBonaFidePuertoRicoResident true) is not read as cleared either —
        see filers:/primaryFilerAttestedNotAPossessionResident and the records contract on
        /flowKnockoutUnsupportedState for the wire and its one-directional scope.

        LOUISIANA IS A MEMBER. Adding it also required adding it to
        filers:/livesInCommunityPropertyState and filers:/domicileStateOptions in
        the same change.</Description>
