              <Dependency module="filers" path="/filerResidenceAndIncomeState" />
            </Right>
          </Equal>
          <Equal>
            <Left>
              <Enum optionsPath="/scopedStateOptions">wy</Enum>
            </Left>
            <Right>
              <Dependency module="filers" path="/filerResidenceAndIncomeState" />
            </Right>
          </Equal>
        </Any>
      </Derived>
    </Fact>

    <Fact path="/writableWashingtonCapitalGainsExciseAboveThreshold">
      <Name>Attestation: Washington capital gains excise base above the 2025 standard deduction</Name>
      <Description>Asked when the filer's residence-and-income state is Washington and the
        federal net capital gain (scheduleD:/netCapitalGain) is above $0. Question: "After
        Washington's own exclusions (real estate, retirement accounts, and the other categories
        RCW 82.87 excludes), is your Washington long-term capital gains excise base above the
        2025 standard deduction of $278,000?" Help text: Washington's capital gains excise (RCW
        82.87) is a 7% tax on long-term capital gains, separate from Washington's personal income
        tax (which does not exist) and from this federal return. Its base is NOT the federal net
        capital gain figure above - Washington excludes real estate, retirement-account
        distributions, and several other categories the federal figure does not separate out, so
        only the filer can say whether the Washington-specific base clears the threshold. Answer
        No if unsure or if the gain is entirely from an excluded category. Unanswered posture:
        defaults to No, complete-safe - the correct answer for the overwhelming majority of
        Washington filers, whose gains do not clear a $278,000 threshold. Validation: Boolean, no
        default answer offered when asked.</Description>
      <Writable>
        <Boolean />
      </Writable>
    </Fact>

    <Fact path="/knockoutWashingtonCapitalGainsExciseAboveThreshold">
      <Name>Knockout: Washington-scoped return attesting a capital gains excise base above the 2025 threshold</Name>
      <Description>Blocks submission when the filer's residence-and-income state is Washington
        and the filer attests (/writableWashingtonCapitalGainsExciseAboveThreshold) that their
        Washington capital gains excise base is above the 2025 standard deduction.
        /scopedStateDoesNotHavePersonalIncomeTax correctly reports that Washington levies no
        PERSONAL INCOME tax, but Washington's capital gains excise (RCW 82.87) is a separate
        state return this dictionary does not compute, does not carry a filing obligation for,
        and does not withhold on. Complete-safe: an unanswered
        state residency, a non-Washington answer, or an unanswered/No attestation is
        unaffected.</Description>
      <Export downstreamFacts="true" />
      <BlockSubmissionOnTrue />
      <Derived>
        <All>
          <IsComplete>
            <Dependency module="filers" path="/filerResidenceAndIncomeState" />
          </IsComplete>
          <Equal>
            <Left>
              <Enum optionsPath="/scopedStateOptions">wa</Enum>
            </Left>
            <Right>
              <Dependency module="filers" path="/filerResidenceAndIncomeState" />
            </Right>
          </Equal>
          <IsComplete>
            <Dependency path="/writableWashingtonCapitalGainsExciseAboveThreshold" />
          </IsComplete>
          <Dependency path="/writableWashingtonCapitalGainsExciseAboveThreshold" />
        </All>
      </Derived>
    </Fact>

